{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0ae8e174c80274e9","type":"text","text":"\n## **11:35** -  Expectations and Seating Plan\n## **11:45** -\tReviewing the test\n## **11:55** - Introduction to Prepositions \n\n## **12:05** - CNN10 \n## **12:15** -\tWrap-up and homework reminder","x":-394,"y":-238,"width":649,"height":235,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1d26597adb0f20bb","type":"text","text":"# Today's Class: Review the test ","x":-414,"y":-314,"width":828,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"2d399b918570d82d","type":"text","text":"# PREPOSITIONS OF TIME\n\n## 1. What are prepositions?\n\nPrepositions are words that tell us when something happens or where something is.\n\nFor time, we often use:\n\nIN, ON and AT\n\nOther examples include:\n\nBEFORE, AFTER, DURING, FOR, SINCE, UNTIL and BY.\n\n## 2. Preposition of time: IN\n\nWe use IN for longer periods of time.\n\n## IN = months, years, seasons, parts of the day\n\n|Use|Example|\n|---|---|\n|Months|in January|\n|Years|in 2026|\n|Seasons|in summer|\n|Centuries|in the 21st century|\n|Parts of the day|in the morning|\n|Parts of the day|in the afternoon|\n|Parts of the day|in the evening|\n\nExamples:\n\n- My birthday is in July.\n    \n- I was born in 2010.\n    \n- We go swimming in summer.\n    \n- I study English in the morning.\n    \n- My parents watch TV in the evening.\n    \n\nExtra meaning: In can also mean after a period of time.\n\n\"The lesson starts in ten minutes.\"\n\nThis means it starts ten minutes from now.","x":-817,"y":214,"width":560,"height":1408,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dcf162bbfe85d2ce","type":"text","text":"## Preposition of time: ON\n\nWe use ON for specific days and dates.\n\n## ON = days and dates\n\n|Use|Example|\n|---|---|\n|Days|on Monday|\n|Dates|on 15 March|\n|Special days|on my birthday|\n|Day + part of day|on Friday morning|\n|Specific day|on Christmas Day|\n\nExamples:\n\n- I have English on Tuesday.\n    \n- The exam is on Friday.\n    \n- My birthday is on 12 June.\n    \n- We play football on Saturday afternoon.\n    \n- I visited my grandparents on Christmas Day.\n    \n\nRemember: If we mention a specific day, we normally use ON.","x":45,"y":214,"width":420,"height":886,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"548559692c0a3808","type":"text","text":"## Preposition of time: AT\n\nWe use AT for exact times and certain expressions.\n\n## AT = exact times and points in time\n\n| Use             | Example                          |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Clock times     | at 8:30                          |\n| Exact times     | at midnight                      |\n| Exact times     | at noon                          |\n| Expressions     | at night                         |\n| Expressions     | at the weekend (British English) |\n| Holiday periods | at Christmas                     |\n\nExamples:\n\n- School starts at 8:30.\n    \n- I go to bed at 10 o'clock.\n    \n- We sometimes study at night.\n    \n- I play football at the weekend.\n    \n- We visit family at Christmas.\n    \n\nNote: American English often uses on the weekend.","x":638,"y":214,"width":466,"height":994,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"63aed6c58e50f5af","type":"text","text":"## Other important prepositions of time\n\n### BEFORE and AFTER\n\nBefore means earlier than something.\n\n\"I eat breakfast before school.\"\n\nAfter means later than something.\n\n\"I do my homework after dinner.\"\n\n### DURING\n\nMeans something happens within a particular period or event.\n\n\"I took notes during the lesson.\"\n\n### FOR\n\nTells us how long something lasts.\n\n\"I studied for two hours.\"\n\n### SINCE\n\nTells us when a period started and continues from.\n\n\"I have lived here since 2020.\"\n\nCompare:\n\n- For five years (length of time)\n    \n- Since 2020 (starting point)\n    \n\n### UNTIL\n\nMeans something continues up to a particular time.\n\n\"I studied until 9 o'clock.\"\n\n### BY\n\nMeans something must happen no later than a particular time.\n\n\"Finish your homework by Friday.\"\n\nCompare:\n\n- I worked until 5 o'clock. (I continued working up to 5.)\n    \n- I had finished my work by 5 o'clock. (My work was already complete at 5.)","x":1197,"y":214,"width":506,"height":1542,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d58161881259a714","type":"text","text":"# PREPOSITIONS OF PLACE\n\n## 1. IN, ON and AT for location\n\nWe use prepositions of place to describe where a person, animal or object is.\n\n## 2. IN = inside something\n\nWe use IN when something is inside an area, room, building, town, city or country.\n\nExamples:\n\n- The books are in my bag.\n    \n- The students are in the classroom.\n    \n- My phone is in my pocket.\n    \n- She lives in Amsterdam.\n    \n- They live in the Netherlands.\n    \n- There is milk in the fridge.\n    \n\nThink: IN = inside or within an area.\n\n## 3. ON = on a surface\n\nWe use ON when something is touching or resting on a surface.\n\nExamples:\n\n- The book is on the table.\n    \n- The picture is on the wall.\n    \n- My phone is on my desk.\n    \n- The cat is sleeping on the sofa.\n    \n- The keys are on the shelf.\n    \n- There is a poster on the door.\n    \n\nThink: ON = touching a surface.\n\nOther uses:\n\n- The café is on King Street.\n    \n- She is on the bus.\n    \n- The information is on the website.\n    \n\n## 4. AT = a specific point or location\n\nWe use AT when we talk about a particular point, meeting place, destination or activity location.\n\nExamples:\n\n- I am at school.\n    \n- We are at the bus stop.\n    \n- My friend is at the door.\n    \n- She is at home.\n    \n- They are at the cinema.\n    \n- My dad is at work.\n    \n- We met at the station.\n    \n\nThink: AT = a particular point or place.\n\n### IN vs. AT\n\n\"I am at school.\"\n\nThis means school is my location.\n\n\"I am in the classroom.\"\n\nThis means I am inside the classroom.\n\nBoth can be correct, but they focus on different things.\n\n### ON vs. IN for transport\n\n- I am on the bus.\n    \n- She is on the train.\n    \n- We are on the plane.\n    \n- He is in the car.\n    \n- They are in a taxi.","x":1848,"y":214,"width":612,"height":2962,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"732a6bc849bb8624","type":"text","text":"![](data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20font-family%3D%22-apple-system-body%2C%20ui-sans-serif%2C%20-apple-system%2C%20system-ui%2C%20%26quot%3BSegoe%20UI%26quot%3B%2C%20Helvetica%2C%20%26quot%3BApple%20Color%20Emoji%26quot%3B%2C%20Arial%2C%20sans-serif%2C%20%26quot%3BSegoe%20UI%20Emoji%26quot%3B%2C%20%26quot%3BSegoe%20UI%20Symbol%26quot%3B%22%20font-weight%3D%22400%22%20data-d-component%3D%22svg%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20style%3D%22color%3Argb\\(237%2C%20237%2C%20237\\)%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20340%20250%22%20width%3D%22100%25%22%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2265%22%20y%3D%2223%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EIN%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%2231%22%20y%3D%2246%22%20width%3D%2248%22%20height%3D%2243%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22none%22%20stroke%3D%22%238a93a2%22%20stroke-width%3D%222%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%2255%22%20cy%3D%2268%22%20r%3D%229%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22179%22%20y%3D%2223%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EON%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22145%22%20y%3D%2273%22%20width%3D%2248%22%20height%3D%2213%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22169%22%20cy%3D%2263%22%20r%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293%22%20y%3D%2223%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EUNDER%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22259%22%20y%3D%2245%22%20width%3D%2248%22%20height%3D%2211%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22283%22%20cy%3D%2276%22%20r%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2265%22%20y%3D%22148%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3ENEXT%20TO%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%2229%22%20y%3D%22183%22%20width%3D%2225%22%20height%3D%2226%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%2272%22%20cy%3D%22196%22%20r%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22179%22%20y%3D%22148%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EBETWEEN%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22140%22%20y%3D%22183%22%20width%3D%2218%22%20height%3D%2227%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22181%22%20y%3D%22183%22%20width%3D%2218%22%20height%3D%2227%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22169%22%20cy%3D%22196%22%20r%3D%229%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22293%22%20y%3D%22148%22%20font-size%3D%2211%22%20font-weight%3D%22600%22%20fill%3D%22currentColor%22%20text-anchor%3D%22middle%22%3EABOVE%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22259%22%20y%3D%22201%22%20width%3D%2248%22%20height%3D%2212%22%20rx%3D%223%22%20fill%3D%22%238a93a2%22%2F%3E%3Ccircle%20cx%3D%22283%22%20cy%3D%22176%22%20r%3D%2210%22%20fill%3D%22%23238b83%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E)","x":2571,"y":214,"width":350,"height":266,"color":"3"}
